  "articleBody": "When your home’s trim gets damaged, the big question is always: can I get an exact match? It’s totally understandable to want your repairs to be invisible, and thankfully, it's often possible with a bit of know-how. The first step is to assess the damage thoroughly. Is it just a small ding, or is a whole section compromised? Next, you've got to document the existing profile and finish. Take clear photos, measure the dimensions, and if possible, find any manufacturer details on the back of the trim. This information is gold when you're trying to source a replacement. Sometimes, it’s about identifying the exact piece or profile; other times, it’s confirming the finish and color match before any work begins. A common mistake is using an approximate replacement that just stands out, so really prioritize finding that perfect profile and material compatibility. This is where detailed product information and damaged-part identifiers come in handy. If the trim is custom, discontinued, or part of a larger, intricate system, that's a good sign it’s time to call a pro. Skilled trim carpenters, like Abraham's crew at HH Remodeling LLC, are experts at precise work and can often replicate or find solutions for even the trickiest matches.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
